==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 5

==Battleground==
*1 [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*30 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 3.33~5 seconds<sup>100f~150f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 136.67 seconds<sup>4,100f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 206.67 seconds<sup>6,200f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 333.33 seconds<sup>10,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Angel Fanboy]] spawns after 400 seconds<sup>12,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The harsh restriction upscales this stage's difficulty dramatically. While your strategy would still be the Awakened Bahamut Chain strategy you used in [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]], the 5 unit limit forces you to play optimally and maximise the value of each unit on screen, especially Bahamut. This restriction also means it's almost impossible to have enough firepower to kill Cruel Angel Clionel before the second Sleipnir spawns, forcing you to endure for Bahamut's downtime, then repeat the Bahamut chain on the Sleipnir again. Thus, this stage requires an immense amount of precision and/or boosted unit levels.

As yet another result of the major restriction in this stage, stackable units, such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and most [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]] can no longer be used effectively.

Finally, make sure you are able to deal with the triple Angelic Gory wave, who could end your run even after you defeat Clionel if you're not prepared.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Given this stage's restriction, Bahamut and his massive damage output is a non-negotiable choice, as otherwise you won't have the sufficient firepower to beat this stage.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - Since most enemies here are Angels, Ramen's singular knockback, high health and resistance against them make him more than ideal for this particular showdown.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] - As a supplementary rusher, Maglev can take advantage of its extreme speed to pin Clionel and inflict extra damage. It even backs this up with the Extra Money ability, which, combined with its full backswing and knockback effects from Trolly Blogger/Sleipnir can either do serious damage or provide a boost to your economy.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] - Cleanerbot's impressive health for its low cost, high speed, singular knockback and immunity to Knockback/Slow greatly aids rush strategies. It can stall Sleipnir, Clionel and Trolly Blogger while buying rushers much more time to inflict damage, though it does have a long recharge time. Its True Form is helpful here, as it is even faster and tankier, but you will likely end up struggling with [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]] more than New Testament, so you'll have to balance your priorities.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - Can Can Cat is a powerful single-target attacker with huge damage at close range. Primarily useful against Angelic Gories, with Extra Money and Move Speed Up Talents allowing it to get even more value for its low cost.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Fishman is a fast all-purpose rusher that can be effective in infiltrating Clionel's blindspot. He becomes even better here, as his strong individual stats makes him comparatively less affected by the restriction,
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Courier Cat's high stats makes him a very strong rusher for this stage, even with the restriction in place.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Kalisa]]: Kalisa is a fast rusher with massive damage to Angels and full backswing attacks. She can fit inside Cruel Angel Clionel's blind spot and nuke the Angelic Gories in no time flat. She is thus ideal for accompanying Bahamut in the chain. Be aware that Sleipnir can either knock her back into Clionel's effective range or stunlock her to death.
*[[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|Guardian Gamereon]] or [[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|The Majestic Zeus]]: Both can tank an ungodly amount of punishment and can help clear out the Angelic Gories and Trolly Bloggers. They can help give you breathing room and even dish out some damage on their own, but be careful of knockbacks from the Sleipnir and Bloggers.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]] - The zenith of Angelic destruction returns again, though a lot worse this time due to the restriction in place, directly affecting his first form and making it harder to support his evolved form.
*[[Sarukani (Uber Rare Cat)|The One-Hit Wonders]] - High range and Strong Against Angels, with immunity to slow and weaken. Ideal for taking on any enemy, though Sleipnir's knockback may pester them.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Yukimura]] - Yukimura can act as a second Awakened Bahamut and assist with rushing down Sleipnir and Clionel. In Abyssal clears, with boosted levels and talents unlocked, he could basically substitute for Bahamut.
*[[Juvens (Uber Rare Cat)|Juvens]] - Excellent health and resistance to Angels combined with dodge allows him to stand his ground, even dodging Sleipnir's pushing attacks often. Offers top-level protection while delivering massive DPS and having a quick enough recharge to keep up if he is destroyed.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]] - Excellent health, is fast enough to enter Clionel's blindspot, can stunlock her with knockback and hold his own against her for a decent while, and is cheap and has quite the fast recharge.
*[[Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sonic]] - Deals Massive Damage to Angels, and has extremely fast speed, making him easy to use and very rewarding.
*[[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]] - Just like in other advent stages, her ability to tank and deal ridiculous damage helps a lot in this stage.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]] - Fairly cheap, tanky, great damage and able to [[Weaken]] the Angels here. Her Weaken pairs extremely well with Awakened Bahamut Cat, as he will be able to take more hits from Angelic Sleipnir and even survive an attack from Clionel. Artist Cat benefits too, as Lunacia's pierce and Explosions will keep the Trolly Bloggers at bay.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Landshaker Kozuchimaru]] - A very solid unit for this stage, with massive damage against Angels, being fully capable of taking down both Clionel and the rest of its supports. His high speed makes it easier to reach the boss's blind spot, and, if that weren't enough, it can take advantage of knockbacks from Trolly Bloggers and Slepnirs to land multiple hits in a very short time.

==='''Strategy 1 (Cheese)'''===
{{Lineup
|Cleanerbot Cat|30
|Maglev Cat|30
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|30
|talent3 = Explosion Lv. 10
|notes = Manic Lion Cat can be used in place of Cleanerbot Cat.
}}

Send Maglev as fast as possible, wait until you have the money for Cleanerbot and time him so he doesn't get hit by Clionel, do the same for Bahamut. Keep sending Maglev and Cleanerbot. Bahamut's Explosions should push Sleipnir behind the base, buying the time to kill Clionel and eventually win the stage. Attack Up and Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]s may be used to make the strategy more consistent.

